#PAGINA LAYER
#String text
Click tiles to measure distances. Lines and tile counts stay on the map until you clear them.\n\n• $b{Click} marks a tile (add as many as you like).\n• $b{$col[255,128,0]{ALT}+Click} starts a detached measurement without clearing the others.\n• $b{$col[255,128,0]{CTRL}+Click} (on the map, or this action) undoes the last mark in the newest measurement.\n• $b{$col[255,128,0]{SHIFT}+Click} (on the map, or this action) clears all measurements.\n• $b{Right-click} leaves measure mode but keeps the overlays.\n\nNumbers are tile steps ($b{Chebyshev}: how many tiles away). Diagonal legs also show the straight-line length. Colors and line thickness can be changed under $b{Options → Color settings}.
